WEBVTT

00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:14.920
<i>Ministry of Foreign Affairs
 negotiator Shindo Kojiro was</i>

00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:19.330
<i>was absorbed by Kado, a huge structure
that appeared at Haneda Airport.</i>

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:24.480
<i>The mysterious being, Yaha-kui
zaShunina, asks for his assistance,</i>

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:28.030
<i>and he becomes the negotiator
between zaShunina and mankind.</i>

00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:33.800
<i>Yaha-kui zaShunina wishes to
negotiate with the Japanese government,</i>

00:00:34.520 --> 00:00:35.930
<i>and the government</i>

00:00:35.930 --> 00:00:40.560
<i>appoints international negotiator
Tsukai Saraka to represent them.</i>

00:00:41.740 --> 00:00:46.610
<i>A conversation with the mysterious
being and mankind was about to begin.</i>

00:02:22.850 --> 00:02:25.160
Wam

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:42.010
Get back behind the ropes!

00:02:42.010 --> 00:02:42.600
Damn it!

00:02:42.990 --> 00:02:44.700
If only I could get inside...

00:02:52.150 --> 00:02:54.180
Can you talk to it?

00:02:55.070 --> 00:02:56.480
I don't know.

00:02:56.990 --> 00:02:58.320
I'll try.

00:02:59.220 --> 00:03:01.250
There's much I wish to tell them.

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:03.010
Shindo.

00:03:24.900 --> 00:03:28.640
All information changes in 
the process of transmission.

00:03:30.370 --> 00:03:34.810
This change is not a good thing 
for the information itself,

00:03:34.810 --> 00:03:36.650
or those who handle it.

00:03:36.650 --> 00:03:38.570
A telephone game?

00:03:38.570 --> 00:03:41.540
Your reply indicates that 90% of 
the information was transmitted.

00:03:45.510 --> 00:03:46.670
This is another method

00:03:46.670 --> 00:03:50.390
of communication that will decrease the 
amount of change in the transmission process.

00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:52.370
I see.

00:03:54.170 --> 00:03:55.670
There's a problem, though.

00:03:56.960 --> 00:04:01.160
Presently, I am increasing the precision by 
limiting myself to linguistic information,

00:04:01.630 --> 00:04:03.010
but attempts to send information

00:04:03.010 --> 00:04:05.210
via sight and other bodily
 senses simultaneously

00:04:05.210 --> 00:04:06.790
increases uncertainty.

00:04:07.250 --> 00:04:08.260
Which means?

00:04:08.890 --> 00:04:12.180
What you experienced 20 hours ago will occur.

00:04:16.310 --> 00:04:17.610
No.

00:04:17.610 --> 00:04:18.860
Don't do that, no matter what.

00:04:18.860 --> 00:04:21.140
I don't want to do it, either.

00:04:21.570 --> 00:04:23.190
My goal is merely to

00:04:23.190 --> 00:04:26.140
transfer information over a wide 
range without having it altered.

00:04:27.480 --> 00:04:31.800
I want you to offer me an appropriate method.

00:04:32.900 --> 00:04:34.370
In other words...

00:04:42.490 --> 00:04:46.390
I am the Ministry of Foreign
 Affairs Foreign Policy Bureau

00:04:46.390 --> 00:04:49.520
United Nations Policy 
Division Primary Official,

00:04:49.520 --> 00:04:51.390
Shindo Kojiro.

00:04:51.730 --> 00:04:54.990
We're gonna have to stay on our toes, then.

00:05:01.960 --> 00:05:03.800
I'm an International 
Negotiator for the Ministry,

00:05:03.800 --> 00:05:07.910
acting on behalf of the Japanese 
government delegation, Tsukai Saraka.

00:05:09.110 --> 00:05:10.090
<i>She's young.</i>

00:05:10.960 --> 00:05:13.410
<i>But I think I can talk to her.</i>

00:05:14.880 --> 00:05:19.670
Yaha-kui zaShunina wishes to speak 
with the Japanese government.

00:05:19.670 --> 00:05:26.300
Our delegation has been given complete 
authority in this matter by the government.

00:05:26.790 --> 00:05:27.690
In addition,

00:05:27.690 --> 00:05:33.310
the Prime Minister and all cabinet officials 
are on standby at the official residence

00:05:33.310 --> 00:05:35.560
and can be contacted immediately.

00:05:36.770 --> 00:05:39.790
It's possible to start 
negotiations immediately.

00:05:40.890 --> 00:05:42.860
As for the location of the talks...

00:05:44.300 --> 00:05:46.260
Yaha-kui zaShunina desires

00:05:46.260 --> 00:05:53.370
that the talks be held publicly, 
with media access available.

00:05:54.610 --> 00:05:57.120
P-Publicly?

00:05:57.540 --> 00:06:02.630
He wants to broadcast our encounter 
with the unknown to the whole world?

00:06:03.020 --> 00:06:04.170
Gonno-san!

00:06:04.170 --> 00:06:06.380
I love you, alien!

00:06:06.930 --> 00:06:08.100
Accept it.

00:06:08.100 --> 00:06:09.440
Prime Minister!

00:06:09.440 --> 00:06:12.140
This is no longer simply 
the government's problem.

00:06:12.140 --> 00:06:16.860
It involves all our citizens 
and all of humanity.

00:06:17.840 --> 00:06:21.400
I have no objection to allowing media access.

00:06:23.180 --> 00:06:24.400
As for the location...

00:06:24.820 --> 00:06:27.220
There'll be press from all over the world.

00:06:27.690 --> 00:06:30.200
If it's indoors, they may 
not all be able to fit.

00:06:30.200 --> 00:06:32.390
Outdoors, then?

00:06:32.390 --> 00:06:34.870
There are safety concerns...

00:06:35.600 --> 00:06:39.680
No, it may actually be better 
to be in an open area.

00:06:41.600 --> 00:06:43.400
Let's make it right here.

00:06:43.400 --> 00:06:44.340
Here?

00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:46.380
zaShunina!

00:06:47.470 --> 00:06:48.490
No objections.

00:07:04.950 --> 00:07:07.650
We've checked all the possible 
sniper points in the area.

00:07:08.060 --> 00:07:10.450
The coast guard is deployed for the sea,

00:07:10.450 --> 00:07:11.750
but what about the sky?

00:07:12.580 --> 00:07:14.660
I'm less worried about security in the air,

00:07:15.490 --> 00:07:17.430
and more worried about accidents.

00:07:19.090 --> 00:07:22.580
Anyone with equipment, 
please get in the left line.

00:07:22.980 --> 00:07:25.040
Security's pretty tight.

00:07:23.640 --> 00:07:28.920
Anyone with equipment get in the left line!

00:07:25.040 --> 00:07:28.920
If there's a time for tight security, it's now.

00:07:35.560 --> 00:07:38.220
So, we're finally meeting an alien, huh?

00:07:38.220 --> 00:07:41.400
Is that an alien, Gonno-san?

00:07:41.400 --> 00:07:42.770
Don't ask me.

00:07:42.770 --> 00:07:44.810
But if it's not an alien, what is it?

00:07:44.810 --> 00:07:47.500
Maybe... he's from the future?

00:07:47.910 --> 00:07:50.230
Humanity's got a bright future, huh?

00:07:50.230 --> 00:07:53.120
Or maybe he's God?

00:07:54.510 --> 00:07:56.070
God?

00:07:56.970 --> 00:07:58.920
I don't think so, but...

00:08:01.920 --> 00:08:03.080
Tsukai-kun.

00:08:03.740 --> 00:08:06.200
How did it feel to fight on the front lines?

00:08:06.710 --> 00:08:10.460
To be honest, not that good.

00:08:10.460 --> 00:08:13.400
It felt like he was in 
control the whole time.

00:08:15.210 --> 00:08:18.600
I mean Shindo Kojiro...

00:08:18.600 --> 00:08:21.350
Not Yaha-kui zaShunina?

00:08:21.350 --> 00:08:26.610
The being named Yaha-kui zaShunina 
is essentially a complete mystery.

00:08:27.360 --> 00:08:31.570
There's simply so little information that 
you can't predict or plan what he'll do.

00:08:31.930 --> 00:08:37.030
It's more like dealing with a natural
 phenomenon than a person.

00:08:38.060 --> 00:08:39.200
But...

00:08:39.630 --> 00:08:44.130
Shindo Kojiro-san should be a human,

00:08:44.130 --> 00:08:46.080
but something seems off.

00:08:46.550 --> 00:08:50.520
He's acting far too calm 
around that strange being.

00:08:51.450 --> 00:08:56.020
I've done a good number of 
negotiations at the United Nations,

00:08:56.020 --> 00:08:58.010
but I've never dealt with anyone like him.

00:08:58.010 --> 00:09:01.100
He can be trusted.

00:09:01.100 --> 00:09:02.310
I don't know.

00:09:03.480 --> 00:09:06.090
People are complicated.

00:09:08.970 --> 00:09:10.360
What is this?

00:09:10.960 --> 00:09:13.100
It's for sitting and resting your body.

00:09:18.800 --> 00:09:21.450
A folding chair doesn't suit you.

00:09:22.370 --> 00:09:23.460
Doesn't suit me?

00:09:25.060 --> 00:09:25.900
Suiting someone...

00:09:26.310 --> 00:09:28.630
An extremely imprecise concept.

00:09:29.250 --> 00:09:32.480
Neither mean, mode, or median.

00:09:32.990 --> 00:09:35.010
It contains a massive amount of information.

00:09:35.970 --> 00:09:38.100
You continue to communicate 
this vague definition

00:09:38.100 --> 00:09:41.640
without either fixing or broadening it?

00:09:42.090 --> 00:09:44.910
I judge this to be a part of
 the development toward

00:09:44.910 --> 00:09:46.720
a faster form of linguistic communication.

00:09:46.720 --> 00:09:48.130
Sorry, my fault.

00:09:48.130 --> 00:09:49.350
Forget it.

00:09:49.350 --> 00:09:51.360
No, I will not.

00:09:51.360 --> 00:09:53.240
It is a good word, Shindo.

00:09:54.520 --> 00:09:58.030
I know something that suits humans.

00:09:59.180 --> 00:10:00.030
What's that?

00:10:08.870 --> 00:10:10.520
Yes, this is Shindo.

00:10:12.730 --> 00:10:13.960
Understood.

00:10:14.670 --> 00:10:15.780
It's time.

00:10:19.090 --> 00:10:23.460
<b>Prime Minister's Residence, 
Large Conference Room</b>

00:10:24.390 --> 00:10:28.510
<i>The Japanese government delegation 
is about to hold talks with</i>

00:10:26.480 --> 00:10:30.230
<b>Haneda, Tokyo</b>

00:10:26.480 --> 00:10:32.520
<b>Japanese Government Holds Meeting With Alien Being</b>

00:10:28.510 --> 00:10:32.520
<i>the mysterious being known
 as Yaha-kui zaShunina.</i>

00:10:30.230 --> 00:10:32.520
<b>Humanity's First Encounter 
with the Unknown
 The Rest of the World Watches</b>

00:10:30.230 --> 00:10:32.520
Live from Haneda International Airport

00:10:34.150 --> 00:10:37.530
<i>The huge object, known as "Kado," appeared at</i>

00:10:37.860 --> 00:10:42.780
<i>Haneda Airport yesterday, 
continues to take up part of the runway,</i>

00:10:42.780 --> 00:10:45.740
<i>and has shut the airport down.</i>

00:10:46.500 --> 00:10:52.250
Passenger Aircraft 777, 
Identical to the Captured Plane

00:10:46.920 --> 00:10:54.970
<i>We've been informed that 251 passengers 
are also being kept within Kado,</i>

00:10:52.250 --> 00:10:54.270
<b>Passenger Aircraft 777,
 Identical to the Captured Plane</b>

00:10:52.250 --> 00:10:57.590
<b>Are the passengers and crew safe?
 </b>Archival Footage of Haneda International Airport<b></b>

00:10:54.270 --> 00:10:57.590
Captain

00:10:54.270 --> 00:10:57.590
<b>Hidaka Yukio</b>

00:10:54.270 --> 00:10:57.590
Co-Captain

00:10:54.270 --> 00:10:57.590
<b>Shinohara Hidehiko</b>

00:10:54.970 --> 00:10:57.590
<i>and there is concern for their safety.</i>

00:10:58.400 --> 00:11:01.090
<i>Kado is causing many problems,</i>

00:11:01.090 --> 00:11:05.650
<i>but it is believed to belong to the being 
calling himself Yaha-kui zaShunina,</i>

00:11:05.650 --> 00:11:07.620
<i>who appeared from within it.</i>

00:11:08.600 --> 00:11:12.060
<i>What is Yaha-kui zaShunina?</i>

00:11:12.900 --> 00:11:15.550
<i>What will happen with the 
problems surrounding Kado?</i>

00:11:15.550 --> 00:11:18.370
<i>Will the passengers be released?</i>

00:11:19.110 --> 00:11:22.190
<i>9:00 PM, April 26th.</i>

00:11:22.780 --> 00:11:26.700
<i>A historic discussion is about to begin.</i>

00:11:38.100 --> 00:11:41.220
First, I wish to rejoice in this meeting.

00:11:41.850 --> 00:11:47.080
<i>Our encounter will bring 
great benefits to the world.</i>

00:11:48.010 --> 00:11:50.810
He has the concept of "rejoicing"?

00:11:49.330 --> 00:11:51.690
First, Yaha-kui zaShunina wishes

00:11:52.350 --> 00:11:58.370
to resolve the information 
inequality that exists between us.

00:11:58.370 --> 00:12:00.440
Information inequality?

00:12:00.440 --> 00:12:04.410
Between him and us humans.

00:12:04.410 --> 00:12:08.700
Does that mean you're 
telling us about yourself?

00:12:09.660 --> 00:12:11.510
Who am I?

00:12:12.080 --> 00:12:13.780
Where have I come from?

00:12:13.780 --> 00:12:15.360
What is Kado?

00:12:16.250 --> 00:12:19.200
I would like to translate these 
answers into human language,

00:12:19.200 --> 00:12:20.710
and explain.

00:12:20.710 --> 00:12:22.640
What do you think?

00:12:22.640 --> 00:12:24.740
It's extremely beneficial.

00:12:24.740 --> 00:12:28.300
Additional information will 
give us room to negotiate.

00:12:29.420 --> 00:12:31.310
We have no objections, either.

00:12:35.250 --> 00:12:39.400
First, I would like to call 
this world "the universe."

00:12:39.890 --> 00:12:43.000
I will use this information 
as a base in my discussion.

00:12:44.570 --> 00:12:48.160
I have come from outside the universe.

00:12:48.520 --> 00:12:49.660
From outside...

00:12:49.660 --> 00:12:50.950
...the universe?

00:12:51.310 --> 00:12:53.950
zaShunina, it would be faster to show them.

00:12:54.720 --> 00:12:55.710
Excuse me.

00:12:55.710 --> 00:12:57.470
We're going to use that water.

00:13:10.490 --> 00:13:12.300
Hey, what's going on?

00:13:12.300 --> 00:13:14.100
That's an arm.

00:13:14.100 --> 00:13:16.030
An arm? Whose arm?

00:13:16.030 --> 00:13:17.430
I don't know!

00:13:17.430 --> 00:13:20.490
Wow! Wow! Wow! Wow!

00:13:20.490 --> 00:13:22.940
I've never seen higher dimensions before!

00:13:38.330 --> 00:13:39.670
What happened?

00:13:43.630 --> 00:13:48.680
I just passed through the outside 
of the universe, my own territory,

00:13:48.680 --> 00:13:49.680
to take the water.

00:13:50.530 --> 00:13:55.180
That territory is adjacent to 
every point in the universe.

00:13:56.310 --> 00:13:59.060
It is called "Novo."

00:13:59.510 --> 00:14:00.890
Novo?

00:14:00.890 --> 00:14:03.800
Translated, it would mean "anisotropic."

00:14:04.250 --> 00:14:05.450
Anisotropic...

00:14:05.450 --> 00:14:07.020
This is how it's written.

00:14:07.970 --> 00:14:12.970
Anisotropic

00:14:08.390 --> 00:14:13.720
Essentially, it's a world with higher
 dimensions than our universe.

00:14:14.450 --> 00:14:17.890
A "higher-dimensional world" would 
be the easiest way to put it.

00:14:17.890 --> 00:14:18.790
Shindo.

00:14:19.770 --> 00:14:21.870
That expression will
 cause misunderstanding.

00:14:22.410 --> 00:14:25.400
The translation "higher-dimensional 
world" is inappropriate.

00:14:26.350 --> 00:14:27.920
"Anisotropic" is most appropriate.

00:14:27.920 --> 00:14:31.320
You said you'd let me handle
 the localization and explanation.

00:14:31.320 --> 00:14:32.910
I want to fix misunderstandings.

00:14:32.910 --> 00:14:35.310
What's important now is speed 
and their acceptance.

00:14:35.310 --> 00:14:38.310
If you're only going to allow what's 
most appropriate, we'll fall behind.

00:14:38.630 --> 00:14:40.600
We can take time later to correct it.

00:14:41.430 --> 00:14:42.620
I accept this.

00:14:42.620 --> 00:14:43.690
Continue.

00:14:56.610 --> 00:14:58.080
That is Kado.

00:14:58.930 --> 00:15:00.810
A boundary object I have manifested

00:15:00.810 --> 00:15:02.680
between this place and the anisotropic.

00:15:03.690 --> 00:15:08.090
Beyond Kado is a world between 
the anisotropic and the universe.

00:15:09.000 --> 00:15:13.470
Kado is a boundary object, but at the 
same time also a transforming mechanism.

00:15:13.800 --> 00:15:15.420
A transforming mechanism?

00:15:15.420 --> 00:15:18.420
The boundaries are highly exclusionary.

00:15:19.120 --> 00:15:22.420
Kado has the processing functions 
required to cross them.

00:15:23.100 --> 00:15:28.790
I am visiting the universe by 
doing the processing on myself.

00:15:29.940 --> 00:15:32.860
However, it is still impossible to 
get rid of all the friction

00:15:32.860 --> 00:15:35.210
and discord that results from this.

00:15:35.740 --> 00:15:40.920
We call this exclusionary 
phenomenon "Fregonics."

00:15:41.400 --> 00:15:42.730
Fregonics?

00:15:43.380 --> 00:15:45.230
Your word?

00:15:45.230 --> 00:15:46.930
Discord. Friction—

00:15:46.930 --> 00:15:48.290
Fregonics is fine.

00:15:54.570 --> 00:15:58.340
First, I made Kado manifest in this world.

00:15:59.060 --> 00:16:05.730
Then, I made a body for myself,
 which made individual action possible.

00:16:05.730 --> 00:16:09.230
As for the passenger plane 
you enveloped during this?

00:16:09.230 --> 00:16:12.110
I want it to be understood 
as a unexpected event.

00:16:12.590 --> 00:16:15.310
I had no choice but to have Kado do the

00:16:15.310 --> 00:16:18.950
appropriate processing in order to 
maintain their biological functions.

00:16:19.390 --> 00:16:22.700
The reverse procedure is 
presently being performed.

00:16:23.650 --> 00:16:28.120
<i>The plan is for all passengers 
to be released within a month.</i>

00:16:28.120 --> 00:16:29.000
Prime Minister!

00:16:30.370 --> 00:16:32.590
That's the first big problem...

00:16:34.500 --> 00:16:36.470
Why did you come to Japan?

00:16:36.850 --> 00:16:40.350
The Unocle is stable here.

00:16:40.900 --> 00:16:42.850
What is Unocle?

00:16:42.850 --> 00:16:47.050
The language to describe it properly 
doesn't exist in this universe.

00:16:47.840 --> 00:16:50.360
If a degree of misunderstanding 
will be allowed,

00:16:50.380 --> 00:16:53.160
there is a word that 
matches approximately 51%.

00:16:55.400 --> 00:16:56.610
"Heart."

00:16:56.610 --> 00:16:58.050
Heart?

00:16:58.050 --> 00:17:01.300
There are multiple vectors inherent 
in psychological activity.

00:17:02.310 --> 00:17:04.750
One of them is Unocle.

00:17:04.750 --> 00:17:07.470
I lack a full understanding myself,

00:17:08.000 --> 00:17:12.410
but perhaps it is similar to the words 
"sympathy" and "sharing" in Japanese.

00:17:12.950 --> 00:17:13.880
Bread.

00:17:14.370 --> 00:17:15.280
Bread?

00:17:15.280 --> 00:17:17.390
Um, I'll explain.

00:17:17.390 --> 00:17:20.530
Let's say there's more bread 
here than we could possibly eat.

00:17:20.980 --> 00:17:23.610
And that we'd eaten our fill.

00:17:24.430 --> 00:17:26.420
Then, a starving person appears.

00:17:27.400 --> 00:17:28.270
What would you do?

00:17:29.090 --> 00:17:30.970
Give them the bread.

00:17:30.970 --> 00:17:32.160
Yes.

00:17:32.160 --> 00:17:33.530
That's what you would do.

00:17:35.000 --> 00:17:37.130
To share that which you have extra of.

00:17:37.130 --> 00:17:41.160
This psychological vector is called Unocle.

00:17:41.500 --> 00:17:43.110
What do you mean?

00:17:43.110 --> 00:17:46.130
All humans would do that,

00:17:46.130 --> 00:17:48.070
but in reality, that isn't what happens,

00:17:48.840 --> 00:17:50.660
because there's a finite amount of bread.

00:17:51.170 --> 00:17:55.230
Many humans in this area are 
capable of sharing that bread.

00:17:55.650 --> 00:17:59.350
That's why I judged it most 
efficient to negotiate

00:17:59.350 --> 00:18:01.550
with the representatives of this area.

00:18:02.870 --> 00:18:07.160
Let me ask another question, 
Yaha-kui zaShunina.

00:18:07.160 --> 00:18:09.770
Why did you come to this universe?

00:18:10.810 --> 00:18:13.690
To advance the world.

00:18:19.200 --> 00:18:21.080
As I said,

00:18:21.080 --> 00:18:24.990
Kado is a transforming mechanism 
between the anisotropic and the universe.

00:18:25.490 --> 00:18:28.730
It changes this world into the anisotropic,

00:18:29.900 --> 00:18:32.790
and changes the anisotropic into this world.

00:18:36.550 --> 00:18:38.010
This is called Wam.

00:18:40.080 --> 00:18:43.530
You would feel like there 
are two of them here, right?

00:18:44.640 --> 00:18:46.430
But these two are one.

00:18:47.570 --> 00:18:49.730
I don't understand.

00:18:49.730 --> 00:18:50.900
What's this?

00:19:03.560 --> 00:19:05.490
Batteries?

00:19:06.390 --> 00:19:10.130
Wam are a device for drawing electrical 
power from the anisotropic.

00:19:16.730 --> 00:19:18.630
Isn't that really dangerous?

00:19:20.120 --> 00:19:24.140
How much power can be drawn from them?

00:19:24.140 --> 00:19:26.390
If I follow Shindo's suggestion

00:19:26.390 --> 00:19:30.000
and prioritize speed and your 
acceptance in choosing my words,

00:19:31.840 --> 00:19:32.810
"infinite."

00:19:34.310 --> 00:19:36.340
What did he just say?

00:19:36.340 --> 00:19:38.320
Infinite energy?

00:19:38.320 --> 00:19:40.680
If you believe what he says,

00:19:40.680 --> 00:19:45.070
this single device is enough 
to power all of human society.

00:19:45.070 --> 00:19:47.830
No, that's impossible...

00:19:48.140 --> 00:19:52.330
I want you to see this so that you 
can understand more precisely.

00:19:52.680 --> 00:19:54.580
Hey, zaShunina, what are you—

00:19:54.580 --> 00:19:55.320
Kado.

00:20:14.810 --> 00:20:16.310
What's going on?

00:20:16.310 --> 00:20:18.770
Haneda's got an uninterruptable power supply!

00:20:19.210 --> 00:20:20.690
It's no good! It's not turning on!"

00:20:21.640 --> 00:20:28.200
I just used Kado to turn off 
all the power to this facility.

00:20:28.200 --> 00:20:31.600
Hey, don't do that without asking first!

00:20:57.570 --> 00:21:02.940
Presently, the Wam is supplying 
all energy to this facility.

00:21:04.910 --> 00:21:08.570
The Wam is more bread 
than you could ever eat.

00:21:10.330 --> 00:21:14.820
I want to offer this Wam to you.

00:21:47.570 --> 00:21:48.740
Mankind,

00:21:49.500 --> 00:21:51.580
I want you to choose the right answer.

00:21:54.120 --> 00:21:57.500
I know something that suits humans.

00:22:02.890 --> 00:22:04.010
Advancement.

00:23:36.550 --> 00:23:40.890
There are countless problems here,
but the Wam are the most pressing.

00:23:40.890 --> 00:23:45.590
The security council considers Japan's 
keeping the Wam to themselves a problem.

00:23:45.590 --> 00:23:47.170
The resolve to drop a bomb.

00:23:47.670 --> 00:23:48.850
Resolve?

00:23:48.550 --> 00:23:52.000
Rotowa
